---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('attentive')!;
const b = appBySlug('recart')!;
const path = '/compare/attentive-vs-recart';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/attentive-vs-recart');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/attentive-vs-recart');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should I evaluate Recart?",
    "answer": "When managed SMS alongside an identified email owner fits the store\u2019s staffing needs and the service approval and suppression handoffs can be demonstrated."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Recart replace the email provider?",
    "answer": "Its managed SMS page describes email marketing partners. Confirm the actual email owner and integration rather than assuming Recart supplies replacement email sending."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Attentive email automatically enabled?",
    "answer": "Attentive documents triggered email journeys but instructs merchants to request access; confirm enablement in the selected account."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these examples prove a winner?",
    "answer": "No. The workflows are proposed acceptance exercises. Compare deduplicated contribution and operator effort with uncertainty before choosing."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Managed SMS release authority beside email: compare permissions, event handoffs and operating cost with your own checkout.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:"Attentive",tool:a.name,reason:"Evaluate email and SMS journeys after confirming channel access."},{label:"Recart",tool:b.name,reason:"When managed SMS alongside an identified email owner fits the store\u2019s staffing needs and the service approval and suppression handoffs can be demonstrated."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Attentive</th><th>Recart</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Operating focus</td><td>Email access and channel ownership</td><td>Managed SMS release authority beside email</td></tr>
<tr><td>Required evidence</td><td>Enabled journey, permission and purchase exit</td><td>Give the managed team a release contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Current channel and service quote</td><td>Current scope plus handoff and staff costs</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Start with the operating model</h2>
<p>Attentive documents triggered email in cart and Shopify checkout abandonment journeys, subject to requesting access. See its <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408727834772-Emails-in-journeys">email journey guide</a>. Compare that combined channel setup with Recart as an SMS service beside your email provider; do not assume either purchase includes every channel and operator task.</p>
<h2>Separate SMS delivery from email partnership</h2>
<p><a href="https://recart.com/fully-managed-sms">Recart’s managed SMS page</a> describes onboarding, migration and campaign work and connects to email marketing partners. Confirm the service included in your quote. Email-provider integrations are not evidence that Recart replaces the email sender, and the page does not establish a push-reminder ladder for this comparison.</p>
<h2>Give the managed team a release contract</h2>
<p>Specify who drafts, approves, schedules and pauses SMS. For a subscription cart, require merchant approval of cadence and offer language; for a bundle whose discount failed, have support resolve the existing offer before approving a new code. Record who can make an emergency stop during a holiday campaign and who checks the next queued send after that stop. Delegating campaign work does not remove merchant responsibility for exclusions.</p>
<h2>Prove the partner email handoff</h2>
<p>Choose one email owner: Attentive with enabled email, or the existing provider connected to the Recart setup. Demonstrate the handoff with an SMS-only subscriber, an email-only subscriber and a purchase between scheduled messages. Use shared customer/cart/order identifiers in the operating record. Inspect both queues after an opt-out or replayed checkout event. Do not infer cross-provider cancellation from a successful email integration login.</p>
<h2>Use high-value objections to test approvals</h2>
<p>For a financing-widget abandonment, route the question to a person who can explain the available payment terms without promising credit approval. For an unavailable size or an incomplete gift message, confirm the purchasable variant and destination before releasing a reminder. These are proposed exercises. The managed team should know when to pause for support and when the merchant has approved resuming marketing.</p>
<h2>Compare the service bill with internal effort</h2>
<p>Request comparable SMS destination and segment volumes, platform commitments, onboarding, creative revisions and managed-service coverage. Include the separate email provider and internal approval time. Compare that total with Attentive’s quoted channel and support scope. A managed arrangement may save operating work, but neither supplier’s attributed-revenue claims establish incremental profit or mobile outperformance for your store.</p>
<h2>Keep incentive economics separate from attribution</h2>
<p>Illustrative $553 basket at 58% gross margin: goods cost $232.26, full-price gross profit $320.74. A 19% order-wide code leaves $447.93 revenue and $215.67 gross profit, a $105.07 reduction with unchanged goods cost. Subtract fulfillment, payment, message and return costs before calling the remainder contribution. This arithmetic is not an observed recovery result or a recommended discount cap.</p>
<h2>Cut over with a measurable decision</h2>
<p>Pause competing recovery queues before enabling their replacement. Reconcile purchase, refund, stock and permission state, save a rollback owner and inspect the return link. Choose timing from checkout behavior and local sending constraints. For a feasible randomized no-message comparison, select allocation and duration from traffic and conversion delay. Deduplicate orders across senders and compare contribution per eligible shopper; a platform-attributed order alone does not establish incremental lift.</p>
<p>Primary product scope checked November 25, 2026. The linked documentation establishes the stated scope; the operational exercises above remain proposals for your team.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
